      "title": "📋 Instructions: UniCanvas 360° Spherical Seam Repair (Full 25-Step)",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 🌐 VNCCS UniCanvas • 360° Spherical Seam Repair (Full 25-Step)\n\n**True Spherical Perspective Editing & Inpainting (No More Roll/Unroll Hacks!)**\n\n### 1. Model Backbone (Full 25-Step Qwen 2.1)\n• **Base Model**: `qwen_image_2.1_Q5_K_M.gguf` (Full 25-step Euler/Simple)\n• **Spherical LoRA**: `pano360_qwen21_edit_v1.safetensors` (strength 1.0)\n• **Text/Vision Encoder**: `qwen3vl_8b_w4a8.safetensors` (W4A8)\n• **VAE**: `qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors` (Wan 2.2 BF16)\n\n### 2. How to Open Your Panorama in UniCanvas\n1. In **[VNCCS UniCanvas]**, click the image import button and select your 2:1 equirectangular panorama.\n2. A prompt asks how to import: choose **\"Panorama\"**.\n3. UniCanvas immediately opens an interactive **1024×1024 perspective editing window** from the center of your 360° sphere!\n\n### 3. Rotate to the Seam or Defect\n• Use the **compact 3D sphere control**:\n  - Drag inside the sphere to turn **Heading (Yaw)** and **Elevation (Pitch)**.\n  - Drag the outer ring to adjust **Roll**.\n  - Scroll over the sphere to adjust **Field of View (FOV)**.\n  - Arrow keys rotate, **Q/E** roll.\n• Turn until the $0° ↔ 360° vertical seam or polar defect is directly in front of you.\n\n### 4. Paint, Mask & Inpaint Directly on the Sphere\n• Select the **Brush**, **Eraser**, **Mask**, or **SAM** (Segment Anything) tool.\n• Paint directly over the seam: *UniCanvas automatically transfers edits into spherical coordinates across the seam and around the poles!*\n• Enter your prompt and click **DRAW** inside UniCanvas to inpaint using the full 25-step Qwen model.\n\n### 5. Inspect in 360° VR\n• Click **Queue Prompt** in ComfyUI: UniCanvas outputs the healed full equirectangular panorama directly into **[🌐 Interactive 360° VR Viewer]** and **[Export 360° Panorama]**!"
      ],
      "color": "#1e3a8a",
      "bgcolor": "#172554"
    },
